--       (hxf : RecRep (2 ^ ℓ) p zf xf) (hxg : RecRep (2 ^ ℓ) p zg xg)
--       (hlf : xf.length = 2 ^ n) (hlg : xg.length = 2 ^ n) (hdf : Disk xf) (hdg : Disk xg) :
--       IRuns I iprog (kronS pM) (encK sB (o0 (gflat zf ++ (gflat zg ++ l))))
--         (encK sB (o0 (gflat (kmulN (2 ^ ℓ) p ℓ (2 ^ n) zf zg) ++ l))) (cKronS p ℓ n BK φ)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFV §49: the Kronecker stage with its parameters (`kronS`)*: `kronS pM = kPushS ; kronU pM ; kPopS`. From the registers `p` (`gPp`), `ℓ` (`gLl`) and `n`
--   (`gNn`) of the base, `kPushS` pushes the record-product parameters of `kronU` (`b = 2p + ℓ + 3`,
--   `r = 2^ℓ`, `ρ = ℓ`) on `50 … 55`, `N = 2^n` on `vRH`, `2 N r` on `vT` and `0` on `vZ`; `kPopS`
--   removes them. **`kronS_runs`**: on `N` records `zf` over `zg` (both disk records at scale
--   `2^p`), the stage leaves `kmulN r p ℓ N zf zg`, which stores `zipWith (ppq r p) xf xg`
--   (again disk records, `p + 1`-bit).
--
